# ── PRIVATE MATERIAL ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ONE RULE: anything not meant for the public — planning docs, strategy,
# pitch decks, brand and GTM material, roadmaps, dev logs — lives under
# `/development-plan/`, which is ignored wholesale. Nothing private sits
# at the repo root.
#
# This replaced a list of ~15 per-file entries. That list was the problem
# it looked like the solution to: every new private doc needed a new line,
# and a doc that got one only after it was written had already been a
# `git add -A` away from shipping. A directory cannot be forgotten.
#
# Public docs are README.md, legend.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, SECURITY.md,
# CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md, LICENSE.md, and benchmarks/parity/README.md.
/development-plan/

# Knowledge-graph output for the internal dev tooling. Regenerated on
# demand and machine-specific; not repo material.
/graphify-out/

# Agent instructions for the internal dev tooling. Kept on disk because the
# tooling reads it from the repo root, but untracked: it points at the
# `graphify` CLI and at `/graphify-out/` above, neither of which a cloner has,
# so shipping it publicly documents a workflow nobody outside can run.
/CLAUDE.md

# Generated build output + stray artifacts (not sensitive, just not repo
# material). Root-level HTML dumps from the dev server and `curl` are
# already covered by the `*.html` rule above, which carries deliberate
# `!` exceptions for the fixture and inspector assets — do not add a
# broader negation here or those exceptions stop meaning anything.
/rustc-ice-*.txt

# napi build output. `npm run build` regenerates the `.node` from source and
# `npm pack` regenerates the tarball, so neither is repo material.
#
# These were tracked until 2026-08-17, and it mattered: a compiled `.node` is
# a 4.6 MB blob that embeds the ABSOLUTE TOOLCHAIN PATHS of whichever machine
# produced it. The tracked copy carried a contributor's home directory in
# every panic string. A committed binary is not just stale weight — it
# publishes wherever it was built.
crates/albedo-node/*.node
crates/albedo-node/*.tgz
